quran[19]{c,v,t}:
  73,1,O you enfolded (in your cloak)!
  73,2,"Rise (to pray) in the night, but (for) a short while,"
  73,3,"half of it or reduce it a little,"
  73,4,"or add to it, and recite the Qur’an distinctly in a measured tone."
  73,5,"Indeed, We shall soon send you a substantial Word."
  73,6,"Indeed, the vigil of the night is more impactful in crushing (the lower self) and more suitable for (creating harmony between the heart and) speech."
  73,7,"Indeed, during the day, you are extensively engaged (in your affairs)."
  73,8,Remember the Name of your Lord and dedicate yourself to Him with complete dedication (detaching your heart from everything else).
  73,9,"(He is) the Lord of the East and the West. There is no god but Him, so take Him as (your) Guardian."
  73,10,"Remain patient over what they say, and keep away from them in a graceful manner."
  73,11,Leave Me with the deniers—(the ones) living in luxury—and give them a little respite (so that their evil deeds may cross the limit).
  73,12,"Surely, We have heavy shackles (for them) and the Blazing Fire,"
  73,13,"and choking food and a painful punishment,"
  73,14,"on the Day when the earth and the mountains will shake violently, and the mountains will become heaps of shifting sand."
  73,15,"Indeed, We have sent a Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) to you as a witness over you, just as We sent a messenger to Pharaoh."
  73,16,"Then Pharaoh disobeyed the messenger, and We seized him with a terrible grip."
  73,17,"If you disbelieve, how will you guard yourselves against (the torment of) the Day that will turn children grey-headed,"
  73,18,(and) the heaven will split apart? His promise is bound to be fulfilled.
  73,19,"Surely, this (Qur’an) is a Reminder. So whoever wishes, let him take the path towards his Lord."
